22. Recommended image sizes and formats

Clients do not have to use one exact pixel size, but keeping consistent image proportions makes the website look correct.

Recommended formats

Preferred:

.webp for most website images

.jpg for photographs when WebP is not available

.png only when transparency is required

Avoid very large original camera files.

Recommended image dimensions

Hero / large clinic image

Recommended:

1800 × 1200 px

Minimum:

1400 × 900 px

Doctor portraits

Recommended:

900 × 1100 px

A portrait-oriented image works best.

Clinic / interior images

Recommended:

1400 × 1000 px

General content images

Recommended:

1200 × 900 px

The website CSS controls the displayed size. The source image should therefore be reasonably large enough for desktop screens but not unnecessarily huge.

Image composition guidance

For hero images:

keep the important subject away from extreme edges

avoid text embedded inside the photo

use good lighting

prefer sharp, high-quality images

For doctor photos:

face should be clearly visible

use consistent portrait style for all doctors

avoid mixing very different crops

For clinic photos:

use clear, well-lit photographs

show reception, consultation area, exterior or key facilities

avoid confidential patient information in the frame

Important

Image dimensions do NOT replace responsive CSS.

Do not change CSS just because a client uploads a different image ratio. First choose a suitable image and let the existing image container/object-fit rules handle presentation.

