Example:

{
  id: "dr-new-doctor",
  name: "Dr. New Doctor",
  specialty: "Cardiology",
  experience: "12 years experience",
  education: "MD, Cardiology",
  image: images.doctors.newDoctor,
}

Do not create an additional copy of an existing image.

27. Adding a clinic

Add another object to:

src/data/locations.js

Required fields:

id
name
address
phone
hours
latitude
longitude
mapUrl

The map will automatically receive another marker.

No component rewrite is required for normal location additions.

28. How to get latitude and longitude

A practical method:

Open Google Maps.

Find the clinic.

Right-click the exact location.

Copy the displayed coordinates.

Put them into latitude and longitude.

Example:

latitude: 28.6139,
longitude: 77.2090,

Use decimal coordinates.

29. If the client has no clinic yet

Keep:

export const locations = [];

The website should continue to work.

The locations section shows an empty state rather than crashing.

When the first clinic is ready, add one location object.

30. If the client has multiple clinics

Add multiple location objects.

Example:

export const locations = [
  clinic1,
  clinic2,
  clinic3,
];

The UI should automatically render:

all clinic cards

all map markers

directions links for each location

31. Before replacing images

Do not simply overwrite a file with a different photo while assuming it is the same asset.

For a new photo:

add one new physical file

add one registry entry

update the relevant data reference

This keeps image management predictable.

